+# Opcode 15: 945 uses across the 20 programs in start.elf, meaning unresolved.
+# Established on hardware: it does NOT write rd (an `add` updates its
+# destination, this leaves it untouched), and it perturbs the configuration
+# space that `ver` reads.  Not named, and given no p-code, until that is pinned
+# down.
+# Opcode 15 writes the codec-register space that `ver` reads.  Measured: it
+# does NOT write rd - reading rd back afterwards leaves it untouched, where an
+# `add` updates its destination - so rd is the DATA, by the same convention the
+# stores use.  The corpus agrees: rd=last 686 times, rd=a register 251, and
+# rd=blank never.  Writing 0x5a5 through it and reading the address back with
+# `ver` returns 0x5a5 for pages 0x300-0x500.
