+# RECOVERED on hardware: the operand is the INDEX OF THE SIGN BIT.  The
+# instruction keeps bits [B:0] and replicates bit B, so B=7 is an int8_t and
+# B=15 an int16_t - which is exactly what the corpus uses (15 in 1431 of 1459
+# uses, 7 in the other 28).  vcedis.php's `sign_extend(rs & mask(B))` reading is
+# wrong: it predicts signext(0x4000, 15) = 0xffffc000, and hardware gives
+# 0x00004000.  Checked against 18 input/width pairs.
